==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Holy Warrior Phoenix''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Head Rococo''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
As a unit, Holy Phoenix suffers from the same issue a good deal of other collab cats do: underwhelming power and a poor choice of abilities; or the inability to fully take advantage of their strengths due to a lack of good range or other reasons. This is true for both his Normal and Evolved Form, as his [[Freeze]] activation rate is only 50% along with terrible uptime for them, making him easily outclassed by more spammable (or consistent) options like [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cat]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] due to their low cooldown and superior attack rates.

==='''True Form'''===
Head Rococo gains multiple improvements that make this True Form a necessity if you intend to use this unit. From over quadruple the effective HP, a better standing range, more synergistic abilities, far higher DPS, and a guaranteed Freeze chance at the cost of his once-short cooldown, he is no longer a failure at what he does. Instead, he now functions as a traditional backline uber that outranges a majority of his targets and can take a beating.

==='''Talents'''===
Head Rococo has an interesting combo of Talents. First up, the '''Defense Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' Talents are good given he is very stat-reliant, but it is generally better to improve him with Catseyes before considering these options. '''[[Immune to Slow]]''' has hardly any notable applications in any relevant matchups and is not worth getting. '''[[Colossus Slayer]]''' looks interesting at first glance, however both [[Mega-Mooth]] and [[Le'Grim]] completely outrange him and deal far too much damage for him to reliably handle; ideally, this would be used on [[Super Hyppoh]], and makes him a decent counter to her stages. Finally, the '''[[Knockback]]''' ability is primarily used to keep the frontline pushers of his respective traits in check, which makes this Talent decent as a supplement to his Freeze against [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, [[Shadow Boxer K]], [[Gory Dark]], [[Razorback]], [[Nimoy Bore]], among others.

